<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
   Android 12+ (API 31 and above). Pre-31 devices read backup_rules.xml instead, which carries the
   same exclusion.

   Entity photos live in filesDir/images/ and are deliberately NOT backed up to the cloud, while the
   database is. The reason is the auto-backup quota: an app that goes past roughly 25 MB stops being
   backed up at all, silently. The image corpus is by far the largest thing this app stores, so
   including it would eventually cost the backup of the ledger — and a photo can be taken again
   where a year of sales cannot.

   Consequence to keep in mind: a restored device has the database but no image files, so every
   img: reference dangles. ImageStore.loadBitmap returns null for a reference whose file is missing
   and every call site already draws its placeholder, so this shows up as entities with no photo
   rather than as a crash.

   device-transfer is left at its default, which includes everything: a direct device-to-device
   transfer has no quota, so there is no reason to drop the photos on that path.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="file" path="images" />
    </cloud-backup>
</data-extraction-rules>
